  era: "1989\u20132014 \xB7 Section 31 \xB7 Independent India \xB7 1947 \u2013 present"
  title: Coalition politics
  text: From 1989, no single party won a Lok Sabha majority for twenty-five years. Coalitions such as the National Front, United Front, NDA and UPA governed, giving regional parties greater influence. A single-party majority returned in 2014.
